{
  "info": {
    "name": "PLG-3146 - APS Graphics Service CRUD APIs use host token",
    "description": "Retest of PLG-3146. The two APIs under Test Cases in the ticket: GET /aps/buckets and GET /aps/models.\n\nBefore running set the collection variables: graphicsBase, twinitToken, nsfilter, apsOssToken, apsViewerToken, bucketKey.\nGet apsOssToken / apsViewerToken with the token script from the Confluence page 'Dev Test Cases - APS' (needs APS_CLIENT_ID / APS_CLIENT_SECRET in the script's .env).\n\nOPEN ITEMS to confirm with Atul/dev: exact Graphics Service base path, how the host token is passed to the service (header name), and the expected status code for the viewer token.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "graphicsBase",
      "value": "https://qa2-api.in.invicara.com/graphicssvc/api/v1",
      "description": "Captured from Reference App network calls on qa2."
    },
    {
      "key": "twinitToken",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Your Twinit/Platform user bearer token (login to qa2)"
    },
    {
      "key": "nsfilter",
      "value": "TestQA2_aW0qOt8s",
      "description": "Project namespace (sent as ?nsfilter=) - TestQA2"
    },
    {
      "key": "apsOssToken",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Token from: get-viewer-token oss"
    },
    {
      "key": "apsViewerToken",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Token from: get-viewer-token viewable (viewables:read only)"
    },
    {
      "key": "bucketKey",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Bucket key returned by GET /aps/buckets"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1 - GET /aps/buckets",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "OSS token (expect success)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Response lists buckets', () => {",
                  "  const j = pm.response.json();",
                  "  const items = j.items || j.buckets || j;",
                  "  pm.expect(items).to.be.an('array');",
                  "  if (items.length) pm.collectionVariables.set('bucketKey', items[0].bucketKey || items[0].key);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{twinitToken}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-APS-Token",
                "value": "{{apsOssToken}}",
                "description": "TODO confirm header name used to pass the host token"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{graphicsBase}}/aps/buckets?nsfilter={{nsfilter}}",
              "host": [
                "{{graphicsBase}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "aps",
                "buckets"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "nsfilter",
                  "value": "{{nsfilter}}"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Viewer token (expect rejected - no API access)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Not 200 with viewer token', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.not.equal(200));",
                  "pm.test('Auth/permission error (401/403)', () => pm.expect([401, 403]).to.include(pm.response.code));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{twinitToken}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-APS-Token",
                "value": "{{apsViewerToken}}",
                "description": "TODO confirm header name used to pass the host token"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{graphicsBase}}/aps/buckets?nsfilter={{nsfilter}}",
              "host": [
                "{{graphicsBase}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "aps",
                "buckets"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "nsfilter",
                  "value": "{{nsfilter}}"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "No host token (expect error)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Fails without host token', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.within(400, 499));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{twinitToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{graphicsBase}}/aps/buckets?nsfilter={{nsfilter}}",
              "host": [
                "{{graphicsBase}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "aps",
                "buckets"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "nsfilter",
                  "value": "{{nsfilter}}"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
